            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Here’s what’s **newest about Azure AI as of today (Friday, July 31, 2026)**, based on public reporting and Microsoft’s own posts/docs:\n\n## 1) Microsoft earnings: Azure growth is being driven by AI demand\nMultiple outlets reporting on Microsoft’s latest earnings highlight **accelerating Azure growth attributed to AI adoption**, alongside heavy AI infrastructure investment. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/other/azure-ignites-microsoft-stock-ai-fueled-earnings-beat-sparks-9-rally/ar-AA294cLq))\n\n## 2) Azure passes a major milestone: “Azure tops $100B annual revenue”\nRecent coverage says **Azure exceeded $100B in annual revenue**, with strong recent-quarter growth also tied to AI workloads and demand—while noting the cash-flow impact of large AI capex. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/companies/microsoft-azure-tops-100b-in-annual-revenue-as-record-ai-spending-cuts-into-cash-flow/ar-AA2903L3))\n\n## 3) Microsoft Foundry (Azure AI Foundry) adds major model + agent capabilities (July 2026)\nMicrosoft’s Azure blog lists a recent announcement: **“GPT-5.6 now available in Microsoft Foundry”** (posted **July 9, 2026**), positioning Foundry as the place to run “frontier” models and production agents with enterprise controls. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/))\n\n## 4) Claude is generally available in Microsoft Foundry (hosted on Azure)\nMicrosoft announced **Claude in Microsoft Foundry is generally available** (June 2026), emphasizing Azure-native governance/procurement and a production path for enterprises. Anthropic also describes how Claude runs with Azure billing/governance, including data-zone options. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/claude-in-microsoft-foundry-is-now-generally-available/))\n\n## 5) Infrastructure expansion to support Azure AI/HPC\nMicrosoft posted about expanding **Azure AI and HPC infrastructure with AMD** (posted **July 20, 2026**), reflecting continued scaling for AI workloads. ([blogs.microsoft.com](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/07/20/microsoft-expands-azure-ai-and-hpc-infrastructure-with-amd/))\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure OpenAI / Foundry Models**, **Azure AI Search**, **Document Intelligence**, **AI Studio/Foundry Agent Service**), I can narrow this to the most relevant “today” items and include the most important links.",
